<br/>This set is excellent for Marksmanship Hunters, providing substantial damage increases through enhanced proc rates and improved ability performance. The 4-piece bonus increases our Ranged Attack Speed, while the 2-piece bonus provides a significant damage boost to Chimera Shot. Prioritize completing the 4-piece bonus as it provides the most significant DPS increase for Marksmanship Hunters in Phase 1.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c3" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/creatureportrait_twilightshammer_dragonegg_01.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Marksmanship Hunter Trinkets in Phase 1</span></h2>DPS trinkets for Marksmanship Hunters in Mists of Pandaria Classic require careful consideration of our rotation mechanics and ability cooldowns. Unlike some classes, Marksmanship Hunters benefit significantly from trinket procs that align with our key abilities. The timing of trinket procs can dramatically impact our damage output, especially when they coincide with our cooldown windows.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>Marksmanship Hunters should generally use two passive trinkets in Phase 1, as they provide more consistent damage output and better synergy with our rotation. The best passive trinkets are <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87167/terror-in-the-mists">
<img alt="Terror in the Mists" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_pvp_trinket.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Terror in the Mists</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87057/bottle-of-infinite-stars">
<img alt="Bottle of Infinite Stars" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_10.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bottle of Infinite Stars</span></a>, however as they can be hard to obtain, there are several excellent alternatives listed below.<br/>
<br/>
<ins>Active Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86043/jade-bandit-figurine">
<img alt="Jade Bandit Figurine" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_rogue_honoramongstthieves.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Jade Bandit Figurine</span></a> is technically the strongest on-use trinket in both single and multitarget content, however it is not recommended for Marksmanship Hunters because of the Haste effect. Haste has limited value for our spec since we don't rely heavily on attack speed, and the focus regeneration bonus is less impactful than raw Agility or Critical Strike procs. Instead, in Tier 14, passive trinkets provide better overall performance and require less micromanagement.</div></li></ul>
<ins>Passive Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87167/terror-in-the-mists">
<img alt="Terror in the Mists" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_pvp_trinket.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Terror in the Mists</span></a> is the strongest trinket available to Marksmanship Hunters in Phase 1. It provides an extremely high damage bonus through its Critical Strike Rating proc, which synergizes perfectly with our damage scaling. The proc has a 115-second internal cooldown and lasts 20 seconds, making it ideal for aligning with our major cooldowns. The Normal and Celestial versions of this trinket are both excellent options as well, with the Celestial version being our best pre-raid option.</div></li></ul>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87057/bottle-of-infinite-stars">
<img alt="Bottle of Infinite Stars" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_10.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bottle of Infinite Stars</span></a> is an excellent trinket for Marksmanship Hunters and your best second trinket. It has a relatively low internal cooldown, making it very reliable. The Agility proc synergizes perfectly with our damage-dealing abilities. The consistent uptime makes it ideal for maintaining steady DPS throughout longer encounters. Unfortunately due to how scaling works, as we move down to the Celestial version, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79328/relic-of-xuen">
<img alt="Relic of Xuen" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_tiger.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Xuen</span></a> is giving it a real run for it's money due to the higher Agility proc.</div></li></ul>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79328/relic-of-xuen">
<img alt="Relic of Xuen" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_tiger.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Xuen</span></a> is a very strong trinket that's easy to obtain and will serve you well throughout Phase 1. The Agility proc provides consistent damage increases and works well with our rotation. The proc has good uptime and aligns well with our ability cooldowns. This trinket is particularly valuable for players who are still building their gear sets.</div></li></ul>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=81267/searing-words">
<img alt="Searing Words" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cat_trinket08.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Searing Words</span></a> is our best pre-raid trinket and should be used until you obtain better options. The Agility proc provides consistent damage increases and works well with our rotation. This trinket is particularly valuable during the early gearing phase, however due to the long internal cooldown, it doesn't match well with our cooldowns.</div></li></ul>
<ul class="exclude-units">
