<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="hit-expertise">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c3" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_marksmanship.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Reaching Hit and Expertise Cap for Marksmanship Hunters</span></h2>In Mists of Pandaria your Hit cap is 7.5% Hit or 2550 Hit Rating and 7.5% Expertise or 2550 Expertise Rating. Keep in mind that some abilities such as the <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/race_draenei_female.gif");'></span> Draenei Racial Heroic Presence will contribute to your overall Hit and/<wbr/>or Expertise needed.<br/>For Hunters, it's especially important to reach both the Hit and Expertise caps, as the stats are also inherited by your pet. This effectively means that they double-dip in effectivity until you reach the cap.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="hit-rating">Hit Rating</h4>At 7.5% Hit, your ranged attacks will no longer be able to miss Raid bosses. This effectively means your key abilities will never miss.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="expertise-rating">Expertise Rating</h4>At 7.5% Expertise, Raid bosses will no longer be able to Dodge your attacks. For Marksmanship Hunters in Mists of Pandaria, this affects both ranged abilities as well as your pets attacks.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="gemming">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c3" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_uncut_purple.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Gemming for Marksmanship Hunters</span></h2>Marksmanship Hunters prioritize Agility above all other stats, as it provides both attack power and Critical strike chance. Secondary stats should focus on Critical Strike and Hit/<wbr/>Expertise. Your gemming strategy should aim to maximize Agility while reaching necessary Hit and Expertise caps.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="q9">Meta Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76884/agile-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Agile Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_metagem_cut.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Agile Primal Diamond</span></a> - Provides Agility and 3% increased Critical effect</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c6">Red Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76692/delicate-primordial-ruby">
<img alt="Delicate Primordial Ruby" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_red.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Delicate Primordial Ruby</span></a> - Pure Agility for maximum benefit</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c11">Orange Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76658/deadly-vermilion-onyx">
<img alt="Deadly Vermilion Onyx" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_orange.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Deadly Vermilion Onyx</span></a> - Agility + Critical Strike.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c9">Purple Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76680/glinting-imperial-amethyst">
<img alt="Glinting Imperial Amethyst" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_purple.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Glinting Imperial Amethyst</span></a> - Agility + Hit, use only if needed for Hit cap or for the socket bonus.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span>Cogwheel Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77541/smooth-tinkers-gear">
<img alt="Smooth Tinker's Gear" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_enggizmos_30.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Smooth Tinker's Gear</span></a> <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77543/precise-tinkers-gear">
<img alt="Precise Tinker's Gear" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_enggizmos_30.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Precise Tinker's Gear</span></a> - When using a Cogwheel gem, generally go for these two.</div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="crafting-professions">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c3" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_mace_39.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Professions &amp; Crafted Gear for Marksmanship Hunters</span></h2>Every profession is viable in Mists of Pandaria Classic as they've been rebalanced to be more equal to each other, however some professions are better than others.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="blacksmithing">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c3" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_blacksmithing.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Blacksmithing for Marksmanship Hunters</h4>Blacksmithing brings with it the now traditional additional Sockets with <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=55628/socket-bracer">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/item_socketedbracer.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Socket Bracer</span></a> and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=55641/socket-gloves">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_addsocketglove.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Socket Gloves</span></a>, giving a flexible stat choice that can be very strong. <br/>We don't get any crafted items from Blacksmithing though, so the sockets are the only real benefit, but it's a strong bonus, as we can choose which gems we put into the sockets. This can give us some flexibility in reaching the Hit and Expertise caps.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="jewelcrafting">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c3" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_jewelcrafting.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Jewelcrafting for Marksmanship Hunters</h4>Jewelcrafting is often seen as one of the strongest professions, and looking at the various <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76734/serpents-eye">
<img alt="Serpent's Eye" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/creatureportrait_sc_eyeofacherus_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Serpent's Eye</span></a>, it's no surprise why. Jewelcrafters can equip 2 <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=83151/delicate-serpents-eye">
<img alt="Delicate Serpent's Eye" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_dragonseye05.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Delicate Serpent's Eye</span></a> for a big jump in Agility.<br/>Combine with the fact that Jewelcrafting is a very accessible profession, and great for moneymaking, it's a great choice for Marksmanship Hunters.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="tailoring">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c3" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_tailoring.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Tailoring for Marksmanship Hunters</h4>While you won't be equipping the things you craft with Tailoring, you will definitely get some use out of <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=125489/swordguard-embroidery">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_rogue_throwingspecialization.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Swordguard Embroidery</span></a>, an embroidery unique to Tailors.<br/>You could even make the argument that it's the best profession bonus a Marksmanship Hunter can get. Definitely worth considering going Tailoring if you're not already.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="crafted-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c3" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_mace_39.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Crafted Gear for Marksmanship Hunters</span></h3>Crafted items are for the most part no longer restricted by profession, meaning that even if you aren't a Leatherworker, you can equip anything Leatherworkers craft. However, certain professions provide unique benefits for Hunters, particularly Leatherworking for Mail armor and Engineering for utility.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=85831/raven-lords-gloves">
<img alt="Raven Lord's Gloves" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_glove_mail_raidhunter_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Raven Lord's Gloves</span></a> is a great option if you're having bad luck with the drops. It's high item level can be very good.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=85830/raiment-of-blood-and-bone">
<img alt="Raiment of Blood and Bone" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_mail_raidhunter_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Raiment of Blood and Bone</span></a> is great if you don't have a tier piece holding you down in this slot.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77536/deadly-retinal-armor">
<img alt="Deadly Retinal Armor" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Deadly Retinal Armor</span></a> is a strong all-round option for Marksmanship Hunters, providing excellent Agility and Cogwheel sockets that lets you build your own item.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=85787/chestguard-of-earthen-harmony">
<img alt="Chestguard of Earthen Harmony" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_mail_reputation_c_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Chestguard of Earthen Harmony</span></a> is great but falls behind slightly with Celestial dungeons, but may be more accessible early depending on your server's economy and profession availability.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79328/relic-of-xuen">
<img alt="Relic of Xuen" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_tiger.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Xuen</span></a> is the strongest trinket you can get before Celestial dungeons, and is certainly worth the investment. It's also one of the best trinkets for Challenge Modes.</div></li></ul>
